<BaseLayout title="Corrections and withdrawals" description="How AI Amigos receives, investigates, versions, corrects, withdraws, and preserves public evidence records.">
  <div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p><h1>Corrections remain part of the evidence.</h1><p class="lede">A material correction creates a new version and preserves the prior record. AI Amigos does not silently rewrite dates, measurements, review decisions, or evidence tiers.</p><div class="empty-evidence"><span class="status reviewed">0 unresolved public corrections</span><h2>No public correction is currently recorded.</h2><p>This is a status statement, not proof that every page is error-free.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Report a correction</a></div><h2>Correction workflow</h2><ol><li>Record the report, affected URL, exact claim, and non-sensitive evidence.</li><li>Acknowledge receipt and assign an owner.</li><li>Preserve the current version and evidence hash.</li><li>Confirm, reject, or request more evidence with reasons.</li><li>Publish the corrected version, date, change summary, and impact on derived records.</li><li>Withdraw affected benchmarks or claims when correction cannot wait.</li></ol><h2>Service target</h2><p>AI Amigos aims to acknowledge a report within five business days. This is an operating target, not a guaranteed response time.</p></div>
</BaseLayout>
